# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local additions (RR Lyrae fork)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# candidates/ is 1.13 GB of rendered light-curve PNGs, regenerable by
# rrlmbft/scripts/plot_candidates.py from catalogs/dp2_hq_class.  Committing
# them would put a permanent 1.13 GB in the history, past the ~1 GB repository
# size GitHub asks you to stay under, and git history cannot be trimmed later
# without a rewrite for everyone who cloned.
/candidates/*

# candidates/candidates.csv and candidates/scores.csv are deliberately NOT
# ignored.  The manifest maps a filename back to a position and a score, and
# scores.csv is hand-entered ratings -- the one thing in the folder that no
# script can reproduce.

# Personal and set-aside rating files.  `scores.csv` itself is committed --
# it has to be, because it carries the is_rrl answer key and lensrater only
# writes three columns when it creates the file itself, so a clone without it
# cannot be graded.  What must not be committed is one rater's answers: a
# `scores.csv` full of the set-builder's own scores arrives half-answered.
# `--reset-scores` moves those to scores.<username>.csv, which this catches.
# The single-dot `scores.csv` does not match this two-dot pattern.
scores.*.csv

# training_set/ has no rule on purpose: 12 MB for 100 images is small enough to
# commit as-is, and loose PNGs render in the GitHub UI and can be linked one at
# a time, which is the point of a practice set.  Rebuild it with
# rrlmbft/scripts/build_lensrater_training_set.py --seed <n>.
